---
import UntranslatedLayout from '~/layouts/UntranslatedLayout.astro';
import { ArrowLeft, ShieldCheck, Database, Megaphone, BellRing } from 'lucide-react';
---

<UntranslatedLayout
  title="Charge Expert Privacy Policy | BeHonor Studio"
  description="How Charge Expert handles local charging measurements and history, Android permissions, AdMob advertising, Firebase analytics and crash reports."
>
  <article class="pt-32 pb-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
      <div class="mb-10">
        <a href="/products/phonebattery" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-primary hover:text-primary/80 transition-colors group mb-6">
          <ArrowLeft className="w-4 h-4 group-hover:-translate-x-1 transition-transform" />
          Back to Charge Expert
        </a>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
          <img src="/images/apps/charge_expert_icon.svg" alt="Charge Expert icon" width="64" height="64" class="rounded-2xl shadow-md shrink-0" />
          <span class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">BeHonor Studio · Android</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4 font-display text-foreground">Privacy Policy for Charge Expert</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Effective date: October 18, 2026 · Last updated: October 18, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-12">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/20">
          <Database className="w-7 h-7 text-emerald-500 mb-3" />
          <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground text-sm">Charging history stays in the app</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-2">Your recorded charging sessions, named charger tests and settings are stored in app-local storage.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/20">
          <BellRing className="w-7 h-7 text-indigo-500 mb-3" />
          <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground text-sm">You control alerts</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-2">Notifications and background monitoring are optional and depend on Android settings.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20">
          <Megaphone className="w-7 h-7 text-amber-500 mb-3" />
          <h2 class="font-semibold text-foreground text-sm">Third-party services disclosed</h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground mt-2">The release app uses AdMob, Firebase Analytics and Crashlytics; not all processing is offline.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-foreground/80 leading-relaxed prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-foreground prose-a:text-primary">
        <p class="text-lg font-medium text-foreground">
          BeHonor Studio (“we”, “our”, “us”) provides Charge Expert, an Android charging monitor. This policy describes which information the app processes, its permissions, how third-party services may process information and what choices you have. It applies to Charge Expert only, not to other BeHonor Studio apps.
        </p>
        <p>The app does not require registration or an account. Charging calculations can run locally, but the released app includes network-based services for advertising, usage analytics and crash diagnostics. Accordingly, we do not claim that the app is entirely offline or that no technical data is collected.</p>

        <h2>1. Charging measurements and local storage</h2>
        <p>Charge Expert reads battery information made available by Android and the device hardware, such as battery percentage, charging or discharging status, current, voltage, temperature, power-source type, charge counter, and cycle count where supported. It uses those readings to estimate charging time, create charging plans, detect charging conditions, and display measurements and alerts.</p>
        <p>Charging-session history, short charger-test results (including user-entered charger or cable names) and preferences such as selected targets, reminder sound, temperature threshold, and appearance settings are stored in the app's private local data. The app does not require cloud synchronization or a Charge Expert account.</p>
        <p>We do not intentionally upload your detailed charging measurements, saved test history, or user-entered charger names as custom Firebase Analytics events or send that information to AdMob as ad request parameters. Android may include some local app data in system backups or device transfers according to your Android backup settings; see section 6.</p>

        <h2>2. Notifications, background monitoring and Android permissions</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Battery information:</strong> used locally to display charging status and calculate estimates. Hardware measurements vary by device.</li>
          <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> with your permission, Charge Expert can display charging status, target-level reminders and high-temperature alerts. You can change notification permission in Android Settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Foreground service:</strong> if you enable background monitoring, the app may use an Android foreground service and a persistent notification while monitoring charging. You can turn this feature off in the app.</li>
          <li><strong>Battery optimization / wake lock:</strong> optional device-level settings may help keep user-enabled monitoring working in the background. You control these settings through Android.</li>
          <li><strong>Vibration and system sounds:</strong> used for alerts, following the relevant Android system settings.</li>
          <li><strong>Internet:</strong> supports the third-party advertising, consent, analytics and crash reporting services described below.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Charge Expert does not request Android microphone, camera, contacts or precise location permissions for its charging features. It does not offer functionality to remotely control or physically stop your phone's charging circuitry. Removing optional permissions can restrict monitoring or notifications, but basic battery measurements remain available.</p>

        <h2>3. Advertising and your consent choices</h2>
        <p>Charge Expert's release version displays banner advertising through <strong>Google AdMob / Google Mobile Ads SDK</strong>. To serve and measure ads, maintain security and prevent fraud, Google's SDK may process network information (including IP address and location inferred from it), device and advertising identifiers, app and device characteristics, impressions, clicks and diagnostics. This processing is performed by the advertising provider and is separate from the locally saved charging history.</p>
        <p>The app uses <strong>Google User Messaging Platform (UMP)</strong> to request applicable advertising consent choices. Where required, a consent form is shown and a privacy-options entry is available in Settings. Ad requests follow the consent information available to the SDK. Opting out of personalized advertising does not necessarily eliminate technical processing required for limited ads, measurement or fraud prevention.</p>
        <p>Learn more at <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Advertising</a>.</p>

        <h2>4. Usage analytics and crash diagnostics</h2>
        <p>The release app uses <strong>Google Analytics for Firebase</strong> to help us understand how features are used, and <strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong> to investigate crashes and improve reliability. Custom usage events include screen views, guide steps, selection of charging-planning modes, charging-test actions and outcomes, and certain on/off setting changes.</p>
        <p>The app's custom analytics events use predefined event names and bounded parameters, such as a screen or operation identifier, test duration, or a Boolean setting change. We do not deliberately attach the battery's measured current, voltage, temperature, charge history, timestamps of history entries, or user-entered charger labels to those custom events.</p>
        <p>Google may automatically process app-instance or installation identifiers, app version, device and operating-system data, event timing, crash traces, exception metadata and similar technical information. Crash reports can contain technical application state. Such reports should not be assumed to be fully anonymous. Analytics advertising-ID collection and automatic screen reporting are disabled in the app configuration; those settings do not prevent separate identifier processing by the advertising SDK.</p>
        <p>Usage analytics and crash collection are enabled in the release build. Charge Expert does not currently provide a separate in-app switch for Firebase telemetry; advertising consent controls are not a global switch for analytics or crash diagnostics. See <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firebase Privacy and Security</a> for more information.</p>

        <h2>5. Sharing and external services</h2>
        <p>When you choose the app's share action, Android opens the system sharing interface with a summary of the charging status. That information is sent only to the destination you select, which may have its own privacy practices. We do not upload charging summaries through a Charge Expert account service.</p>
        <p>Google processes information needed to provide advertising, consent, analytics and diagnostics. We may receive information you voluntarily send when contacting support, including your email address and the content of your message. We do not sell your saved charging history or charger labels.</p>

        <h2>6. Retention, deletion and Android backups</h2>
        <p>You can clear charging history and saved test information using the relevant in-app actions. Uninstalling the app or clearing its Android app storage normally removes the app's local database and settings from that device. Data you explicitly shared elsewhere is not deleted by removing Charge Expert.</p>
        <p>Charge Expert currently allows Android system backup and device transfer. Depending on the Android version, your backup settings and the system provider, local app data may be included in a cloud backup or transferred to another device and later restored. You can review or disable Android backup through the device's system settings. Removing local data does not necessarily remove prior operating-system backups.</p>
        <p>Advertising, analytics and diagnostic information processed by Google is subject to Google's retention policies and applicable project settings. Uninstalling Charge Expert does not instantly delete information previously processed by third-party services. Contact us for assistance with privacy requests.</p>

        <h2>7. Security and international processing</h2>
        <p>Local records are stored within Android's app storage, subject to device security and backup settings. Third-party network services use their own security controls and may process technical data outside your country. No storage or transmission system can be guaranteed completely secure.</p>

        <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>Charge Expert is a general-purpose utility and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly request personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided information through a support request, contact us.</p>

        <h2>9. Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>You may adjust Android notification, foreground activity and battery-optimization settings; disable app monitoring; manage advertising privacy options where available; clear local data; or uninstall the app. Depending on your jurisdiction, you may also have rights to request access, deletion, correction, restriction or other treatment of your personal data, or withdraw consent where applicable. Contact us to make a request; third-party service requests may require coordination with the provider.</p>

        <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy to reflect app features, legal requirements or third-party services. The latest version will appear on this page with a revised date.</p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>For privacy questions or requests concerning Charge Expert, contact BeHonor Studio at <a href="mailto:beehonorstu@gmail.com">beehonorstu@gmail.com</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-foreground/10 flex gap-3 items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <ShieldCheck className="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-500 shrink-0" />
        <span>This is the privacy policy for the Charge Expert Android app, not the general BeHonor Studio website policy.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</UntranslatedLayout>
